  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "bo_c",
      "defType": "meta/comment",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": -364
      },
      "params": {
        "text": "Breakout\n\nClick the preview to start, then move the mouse left and right to steer the paddle; click again to launch each ball. Break every brick to go up a level (the ball gets faster); three balls, then click to play again. Until you click, the game plays itself.\n\nHow it works: the game is state, held by State nodes and wired with visual nodes only. Turns (open it with a double-click) decides when a game starts, when the ball launches, and counts lives, score and level. Ball moves the ball by its velocity and bounces it off the walls, the paddle and broken bricks. Bricks tests the ball against all 60 bricks at once with Hit Test and remembers which still stand. HUD draws the score, the balls left and the message. Sparks fly from broken bricks.",
        "width": 460,
        "height": 300
      }
    },
